[ceiling] These are the zip-tie channels under the suction-chain, discharge-chain and fluid-14 anchor ribs. Each roof bridges the 3.5 mm channel along X between two complete 3 mm feet; the 23.4 mm or 12.75 mm transverse extent is the rib's width, not its unsupported span. The 3 mm-high channel admits the tie beneath the seated body and remains open at both mouths.
