[ceiling] These are the zip-tie windows through the fluid-18 and water-3 side anchors. Each roof bridges 3.5 mm along Y between complete 3 mm flanks. After the back-channel relief, the roofs extend 28.8 mm along X at fluid-18 and 8.3 mm at water-3. The short space below the roof is the tie's required passage (3 mm for fluid-18 and 1.225 mm for water-3), not a cavity intended to receive a support body.
